        "mission_intent": "Subject: Attorney Up-the-Ladder Reporting Protocol \u2013 Compliance Review Needed\n\nTeam, as part of our broader SOX compliance refresh, I need Legal and Internal Audit to jointly develop and document our internal protocol governing outside and in-house attorneys' obligations when they encounter evidence of a material securities law violation or breach of fiduciary duty while representing us before the SEC. Specifically, the protocol should map out the escalation chain starting with the initial report to the Chief Legal Officer or CEO, and then define the secondary escalation path to the audit committee if the initial recipient fails to respond appropriately with remedial measures. Please ensure the protocol aligns with the SEC's professional conduct rules for attorneys appearing and practicing before the Commission, and coordinate with our outside counsel to confirm their engagement letters reflect these obligations. I'd like a draft framework circulated to the Disclosure Committee for review by the end of next month. Make sure we address documentation and evidence-retention requirements at each escalation step, and include a decision matrix for what constitutes an \"appropriate response\" from the CLO or CEO so attorneys have clear guidance on when secondary escalation is triggered.",
